[TEMPORARY - DEBUG ONLY] Log IPC instance values read by the PMD

Dump the IPC metadata offset/size, the Geul signature, the initialized flag
and the raw max_*_feca_queues values as read from the shared IPC structure,
to diagnose why the PMD reports 0 LDPC queues while the modem firmware
unconditionally writes MAX_LDPC_DEC_FECA_QUEUES=8.

To be removed once the root cause is identified.

diff --git a/drivers/baseband/la12xx/bbdev_la12xx.c b/drivers/baseband/la12xx/bbdev_la12xx.c
index e6e7480..048eb11 100644
--- a/drivers/baseband/la12xx/bbdev_la12xx.c
+++ b/drivers/baseband/la12xx/bbdev_la12xx.c
@@ -2808,6 +2808,14 @@ setup_la12xx_dev(struct rte_bbdev *dev)
 		(&ipc_md->instance_list[ipc_priv->instance_id]);
 
 	instance = ipc_priv->instance;
+
+	rte_bbdev_log(ERR, "DBG off=0x%x sz=0x%x sig=0x%08x init=0x%08x",
+    		mhif->ipc_regs.ipc_mdata_offset, mhif->ipc_regs.ipc_mdata_size,
+    		ipc_md->ipc_geul_signature, instance->initialized);
+	rte_bbdev_log(ERR, "DBG raw dec=0x%08x enc=0x%08x raw=0x%08x depth=0x%08x",
+    		instance->max_ldpc_dec_feca_queues, instance->max_ldpc_enc_feca_queues,
+    		instance->max_raw_queues, instance->max_channel_depth);
+
 	priv->max_queues = instance->max_ldpc_dec_feca_queues +
 		instance->max_ldpc_enc_feca_queues +
 		instance->max_polar_enc_feca_queues +
